{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the number of values of \\( x \\) in the interval \\([0, \\pi]\\) that satisfy the equation \\(\\sin^{-1}(\\sin 6x) = \\cos^{-1}(\\cos x)\\).\n\nFirst, let's analyze the right-hand side of the equation. The function \\(\\cos^{-1}(\\cos x)\\) returns the angle in the interval \\([0, \\pi]\\) whose cosine is \\(\\cos x\\). Therefore, \\(\\cos^{-1}(\\cos x) = x\\) if \\(x \\in [0, \\pi]\\).\n\nSo, the equation simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sin^{-1}(\\sin 6x) = x\n\\]\nThis implies that \\(6x\\) must be in the interval \\([- \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\) plus any integer multiple of \\(2\\pi\\), but since \\(x \\in [0, \\pi]\\), we only need to consider the principal range of the \\(\\sin^{-1}\\) function. Therefore, \\(6x\\) must be in the interval \\([- \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\) or shifted by \\(2k\\pi\\) for some integer \\(k\\) such that \\(6x\\) remains within the principal range of the \\(\\sin^{-1}\\) function when considering the periodicity. However, since \\(x \\in [0, \\pi]\\), the only relevant interval is \\([- \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}]\\).\n\n","prefix_end":1042,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,1372,315,2750,315,17767,856,1124,8,304,279,9873,1124,2561,15,11,1124,2493,17960,8,429,26553,279,23606,1124,11520,15940,87210,16,92,11520,15940,220,21,87,8,284,1124,9407,87210,16,92,11520,9407,856,10699,3593,5338,11,1077,594,23643,279,1290,24413,3108,315,279,23606,13,576,729,1124,11520,9407,87210,16,92,11520,9407,856,10699,8,4675,279,9210,304,279,9873,1124,2561,15,11,1124,2493,17960,8,6693,75259,374,1124,11520,9407,856,59,568,15277,11,1124,11520,9407,87210,16,92,11520,9407,856,8,284,856,57758,421,17767,87,1124,258,508,15,11,1124,2493,17960,3593,4416,11,279,23606,15491,9606,311,510,59,9640,59,15940,87210,16,